## The embed Package

The `embed` package (Go 1.16+) lets us **embed files and directories into a Go binary** at compile time. This means applications can be distributed as a **single binary** without needing external files.

## Embedding a Single File

```go
package main

import (
	_ "embed" // import for side effects
	"fmt"
)

//go:embed hello.txt
var greeting string

//go:embed version.txt
var version []byte

func main() {
	fmt.Println(greeting)
	fmt.Println("Version:", string(version))
}
```

## Embedding Directories with embed.FS

Use `embed.FS` to embed entire directories:

```go
package main

import (
	"embed"
	"fmt"
	"io/fs"
)

//go:embed static
var staticFiles embed.FS

//go:embed templates
var templateFiles embed.FS

func main() {
	// Read a file from the embedded FS
	data, err := staticFiles.ReadFile("static/style.css")
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Println("Error:", err)
		return
	}
	fmt.Println("CSS:", string(data))

	// List all files
	fs.WalkDir(staticFiles, ".", func(path string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {
		if err != nil {
			return err
		}
		fmt.Println(path)
		return nil
	})
}
```

## Serving Static Files over HTTP

```go
package main

import (
	"embed"
	"io/fs"
	"net/http"
)

//go:embed web/dist
var webDist embed.FS

func main() {
	// Create a sub-filesystem from web/dist
	dist, _ := fs.Sub(webDist, "web/dist")

	mux := http.NewServeMux()

	// Serve static files
	mux.Handle("/", http.FileServer(http.FS(dist)))

	// API routes
	mux.HandleFunc("/api/health", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		w.Write([]byte(`{"status":"ok"}`))
	})

	http.ListenAndServe(":8080", mux)
}
```

## Glob Patterns for Multiple Files

```go
//go:embed configs/*.json
var configs embed.FS

//go:embed *.html templates/*.html
var templates embed.FS
```

> **Note:** Files starting with `.` or `_` are not embedded by default. Use `all:` to include everything:
```go
//go:embed all:web/dist
var webDist embed.FS
```

starterCode:
package main

import (
	"embed"
	"fmt"
	"strings"
)

// Simulate embedded files using embed.FS
// In a real project, these would be actual files on disk

//go:embed lesson-04.json
var selfContent embed.FS

func main() {
	// Read the embedded file
	data, err := selfContent.ReadFile("lesson-04.json")
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Println("Error reading embedded file:", err)
		return
	}

	// Count lines
	lines := strings.Split(string(data), "\n")
	fmt.Printf("Embedded file has %d lines\n", len(lines))
	fmt.Printf("First 80 chars: %.80s...\n", string(data))

	// List all embedded files
	entries, _ := selfContent.ReadDir(".")
	fmt.Println("\nEmbedded files:")
	for _, e := range entries {
		info, _ := e.Info()
		fmt.Printf("  %s (%d bytes)\n", e.Name(), info.Size())
	}
}
